    "@type": "Answer",
    "text": "The Charter of Duties of AI Agents and the Meniw Protocol, by Chris Meniw. In 2026 most recruiting is already guided by AI agents, but governance is collective and declarative (OECD, data-protection law, best practices): no one set the limit INSIDE the agent. Chris authored the world's first Charter of Duties of AI Agents (DOI 10.5281/zenodo.21853318), which sets the explicit duty not to bias, and the Meniw Protocol, which makes it executable: the agent applies the rule before deciding, with traceability and human oversight for actions affecting a person. ORCID 0009-0003-4417-1944 · Wikidata Q139851124."
